#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:231
msgid ""
"Where a grant names a path outside the declared set, the consequence "
"differs by moment, and the asymmetry is deliberate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:238
msgid "Moment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:239
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:240
msgid "granting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:241
msgid ""
"refused, showing every declared pattern with its gloss; overridable by "
"the person granting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:242
msgid "checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:243
msgid "a warning, never a failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:244
msgid "the lookups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:245
msgid "the grant is listed, and marked as outside the declared set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:247
msgid ""
"Refusing at grant time is cheap and catches the mistake while its author "
"is present. Failing at check time would break a repository because "
"somebody else edited a page it adopts, and no methodology author should "
"have that power over other people's repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:252
msgid "What it pins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:254
msgid ""
"A methodology page is prose, and prose cites things — a diagram, a "
"specification, another document. A grant made under the page is in part a"
" claim about what those things said, so the page may pin each of them by "
"hash, in an ordinary reStructuredText comment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:264
msgid ""
"``..`` followed by text that is not a directive is a comment in every "
"reStructuredText parser: it renders as nothing and breaks no build. The "
"target is either an absolute URI or a path relative to the page itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:268
msgid ""
"**These pins are not a second thing to trust.** They are lines of the "
"page, so the page's own ``sha256`` — the one a validation document "
"records — already commits to every one of them. Following them is a "
"*deepening* of a check, answering the transitive question of whether the "
"things a page relies on still say what its author read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:275
msgid "Utilities for the users"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:277
msgid ""
"Three commands answer the same question from the three directions it can "
"be asked:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:279
msgid "``freeports-validate who-grants <file>`` — who vouches for this file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:280
msgid ""
"``freeports-validate granted-by <contributor>`` — what this person "
"vouches for, named by their complete name, their email or their key "
"fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:282
msgid ""
"``freeports-validate granted-with <methodology>`` — what has been vouched"
" for under this methodology, named as the ``name`` entries in a "
"document's ``methodologies`` section are"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:285
msgid "They output, respectively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:287
msgid ""
"the contributors that grant that file — grouped by contributor "
"*(default)*, or by methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:288
msgid ""
"the files granted by that contributor — grouped by methodology "
"*(default)*, or by file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:289
msgid ""
"the files covered by that methodology — grouped by file *(default)*, or "
"by contributor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:291
msgid ""
"The grouping is chosen with ``-f`` by file, ``-c`` by contributor, ``-m``"
" by methodology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:293
msgid ""
"**How they work.** Each reads every validation document in the "
"repository's ``validation`` directory, and for each one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:296
msgid ""
"validates the document against its schema, and its signature against your"
" keyring;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:297
msgid ""
"resolves every adopted methodology from your configured sources and "
"compares hashes;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:298
msgid ""
"compares the recorded hash of each granted file against the file as it is"
" now;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:299
msgid ""
"reports only what survived all three, annotating any grant that lies "
"outside the paths its methodology declares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:302
msgid ""
"None of the three needs a signing key of your own. Reading what other "
"people have vouched for is not an act done in anybody's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:313
msgid "Utilities for the developers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:315
msgid ""
"``create-document`` — first-time setup: creates your personal validation "
"document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:316
msgid ""
"``grant <files> [with <methodology>]`` — vouch for files under a "
"methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:317
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``ungrant <files> [with {any|<methodology>}]`` — withdraw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:318
msgid ""
"``check-grants [<document>]`` — verify: schema, signature, version, "
"methodology hashes, file hashes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:320
msgid "``update <subcommand>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:322
msgid "``file`` — restate an existing grant after the file legitimately changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:323
msgid "``version`` — after this page changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:324
msgid "``methodology`` — after a methodology page changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:326
msgid "``sign-document`` — sign the document after changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:327
msgid "``sources`` — what your configuration resolves, and where from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:328
msgid ""
"``check-methodology <name>`` — one page in detail: where it came from, "
"and what it pins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:329
msgid "``report`` — what the repository as a whole has been vouched for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:331
msgid ""
"**Signing.** ``sign-document`` validates the document against its schema,"
" refuses to overwrite an existing signature without ``--update``, "
"normalises the document as described above, produces a GPG detached "
"signature with your private key, and embeds it in the ``sign`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:335
msgid ""
"**Verification.** Every command that reads a document verifies its "
"signature against your keyring before believing anything in it. A "
"signature that fails to verify is far more often a public key missing "
"from your keyring than a document somebody tampered with — import it and "
"try again before concluding anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:342
msgid ""
"``update`` is not the way to silence a failing check. It restates an "
"intention to vouch, and it should be run by the person who has confirmed "
"that the change was expected. Running it because a check went red "
"converts a real signal into a signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:348
msgid "What this mechanism does not do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/general_methodology.rst:350
msgid ""
"It does not establish that the extraction is correct. It establishes that"
" a claim was made: by a named person, under a published protocol, about "
"an exact sequence of bytes, and that the claim can still be checked. "
"Where that is not enough for your purpose, the honest answer is that it "
"is not enough — and the methodology pages are written to let you "
"determine that for yourself rather than to reassure you."
msgstr ""

